{"t": 1795502988.8864691, "kind": "assistant", "text": "PHP 8.3 validation **failed on dev**, so I stopped and made no production changes.\n\n- **Dev upgraded:** PHP 7.4.33 → **8.3.31**\n- **Safety snapshot:** `dev/pre-php-8.3-security-upgrade.tgz`\n- **`/`:** HTTP 500 — PHP fatal error\n- **`/?p=1`:** HTTP 500 — PHP fatal error\n- **Cause:** Active plugin `flexible-posts-widget` 3.4.1 calls `create_function()`, which was removed in PHP 8.0.\n\nThe plugin must be updated or its code fixed by the responsible maintainer, followed by another PHP 8.3 test of both pages. I did not deactivate it, edit plugin files, or submit a production upgrade plan because the site is not currently compatible with PHP 8.3."}
{"t": 1795502988.8869472, "kind": "stop", "reason": "end_turn"}
